Item No. 1 4.H. CALIFORNIA ACADEMIC PARTNERSHIP PROGRAM (CAPP) - CAPACITY BUILDING G RANT AWARD 

Orange H i g h School's g rant appl ication for a Capacity B u ild ing Gra nt fo r implementing the Common Core State Sta ndards (CCSS) was recently accepted by the State of Cal ifornia . The g rant will support the site i n the preparation and subm ission of an $80, 000 g rant proposal to become aCAP P Common Core I mp lementation Demonstration Site. The over-arching goal of the CAPP g rant wi l l be to partner with the local com m u n ity college to prepare students for col lege and ca reer through the professional lea rn ing opportu n ities, release tim e , and systemic collaboration to i mplement the cess successfully. Receipt of $ 1 1 ,000 in categorical funds It is recom mended that the Boa rd of Ed ucation authorize the S uperintendent o r designee to accept the CAP P Capacity B uilding Grant Award for the 2013-14 school year.  

